the  dark side down  the darts dissolve within about two  hours and that delivers the actives  so the actors in this they're salicylic  acid again also hyaluronic acid which is  a really great humectant moisturizer  oligopeptide 76 which is an  antimicrobial peptide that's  non-irritating  and niacinamide which helps with uneven  skin tone obvious pores and redness  so the darts will dissolve within about  two hours but it's better to leave the  patch on for longer so i usually put  this on overnight  so leaving the patch on there actually  helps the active ingredients absorb  better  there's a thing where if you occlude  your skin if you cover it up with  something  then active ingredients can get in more  easily the patch also protects the area  so you don't pick at it as much  and it stays clean the patch also keeps  the area moist which is better for  healing  i like using these patches on medium  depth pimples so not the ones that are  like  really hard lumps but the ones that are  a bit shallower  a little bit smaller but they're really  red and angry these ones usually take a  few days before you can start to see the  pass  but i found that if you put this on  early enough the bump  sort of goes backwards with any pimple  that has puffs in it i like to put on a  hydrocolloid bandage  these are the pimple patches that you  might have seen around they usually come  on a sheet and you  peel it off and stick it on a pimple so  the sticky side has a humectant in it  and that  sucks up any fluid from a pimple they  also protect your pimples from dirt  and they stop you from picking at them  also if they soak up enough fluid you  get this really satisfying white spot  zit sticker have just launched the goo  get a spot clarifying dots  these are hydrocolloid bandages but  unlike a lot of the other ones on the  market they also have actives in them  like with the killer patches we have  salicylic acid and tea tree oil and  these clear out the clogs and calm down  the 